# configure/networking.md: NETWORK SETTINGS, the Wi-Fi picker, a saved
# network's dialog and SAVED NETWORKS. Needs the stand-in wifictl (README).
# NETWORK SETTINGS is six presses up from the MAIN MENU's top row (BACK,
# QUIT, SYSTEM SETTINGS, UPDATES & DOWNLOADS, SCRAPER, NETWORK SETTINGS); on
# it, WI-FI NETWORK is five presses down from IP ADDRESS and MANAGE SAVED
# NETWORKS two more. In the picker the stand-in lists Home Wi-Fi (in use)
# first, Cafe (saved) second and Neighbour third; a press on Neighbour opens
# the WI-FI KEY keyboard, where every key is a letter, so the count to Cafe
# is one down, never two (the third capture typed "zz" into it).
# The MAIN MENU is reached from its bottom, so the walk is the same whether
# the guest is signed in to RetroAchievements (the menu then opens on that
# row, above GAME SETTINGS) or not: up from the top row lands on BACK, the
# next on QUIT, and the rows above QUIT never move. (Until EmulationStation
# f1ae6bc25 the first press landed on an empty tab strip, #325, and every
# count here was one higher.)
key ret
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
key up
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot network-settings
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
wait 5
settle
shot wifi-networks
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot wifi-saved-network
key z
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key z
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
key down
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
wait 3
settle
shot saved-networks
key x
wait-for-change 30 1
settle
shot forget-network
dismiss-dialogs
